00:00:02.899 --> 00:00:05.059 align:start position:0%
Devil May Cry 5 isn't shy about being a  pure celebration of the series's past  while it has plenty of new ideas this  latest sequel is laced with entertaining  callbacks that are sure to bring a smile  to your face in addition there's a  surprising amount of extended universe  lore acknowledged in DMC 5 that even  hardcore fans might not recognize for  your entertainment and general amusement  we've compiled the most noteworthy  Easter eggs and references in DMC 5 be  wary there are some lights or others  ahead anyway let's get on to it shall we  the city of Redgrave is a nod to Tony  Redgrave which is Dante's alias in the  anime and early light novels in a note  in the gallery menu this element is  reintroduced into the Canon  explaining that Dante took on the name  since Redgrave City is his hometown the  name Tony Redgrave itself is a nod to  Capcom's past as it's Dante's original  name back when dmc1 was being developed  as Resident Evil 4  [Music]  throughout the story Nikko continually  brings up Nell Goldstein her grandmother  and legendary gunsmith my grandmother  was called the 45 caliber virtuoso  legendary goes me I hope to be like her  someday  an artist known as the 45 caliber  virtuoso Nell originates from a Devil  May Cry light novel she and Dante who  went by Tony at the time are established  in the book as close friends the  fledgling demon hunter would often stop  by Nell shop to buy new guns as well as  sell any spares he picked up but during  his jabs Dante would often break his  pistols so Nell decided to craft for him  the indestructible dual pistols a beanie  and ivory to solve this persistent  annoyance after Devil May Cry threes  released details in that game's story  ended up contradicting the events of  that novel and as a result were removed  from the Canon however JD Morrison's  letters to Nero Indy mc5 end up bringing  a lot of the novel's elements back into  the Canon including Nell goldstein  speaking of JD Morrison he originates  from Delhi May Cry the animated series a  small 12-episode anime that ran back in  2007 unlike the novel the anime is canon  taking place after dmc1 and introducing  Morrison as Dante's agent who brings him  job requests  don't forget I'm counting on you though  the Morrison in the show features a  completely different design from the  game another character introduced in the  anime is patty Lowell a young girl that  ends up in Dantes care and lives in the  Devil May Cry shop for a time she makes  a voiced appearance in DMC 5 calling up  Dante to invite him to her 18th birthday  party  [Music]  how does it feel to be rescuing the guy  that killed your father  well he abandoned my mother and I left  us for dead Nico's father is mentioned a  few times throughout the mc5 but it's  never explicitly stated who he is  but if you research the gallery enough  you can find several notes pointing to  his identity profile that Nikko wrote up  on dark nights Sparta mentions that her  father was from Fortuna which is the  primary setting of DMC for in addition  the Red Queen weapon report states that  Nico's father has designed the blade if  there's anyone from previous games who  most fits the bill based on these clues  it's Agnes the smarmy researched  obsessed scientist from DMC for soon  this lines up with details confirmed  about Nico's father early on who was  said to be killed by Dante and given  Nico's general disdain for her father it  makes the most sense that it's Agnes  [Music]  the Cavalier is likely a callback to the  series's love of inserting motorcycles  into action scenes specifically in dmc1  and dmc3 this crazy Chainsaw motorcycle  is earned after defeating Cavalier  Angelo which is the boss that Trish was  trapped inside getting the Cavalier  after this fight in particular is  fitting given Trish's association with  motorcycles she did crash into Dante's  office with one in dmc1 after all  [Music]  if you didn't recognize them already  these familiars shadow Griffin and  nightmare are direct nods to dmc1 bosses  of the same names in fact many of their  attacks and animations are lifted  straight from those bosses for example  shadows bayonet attack is very similar  to the attack that it's dmc1 counterpart  opens up its boss fight with you'll even  notice later on that much of mission 18  features several call backs of each  familiars dmc1 counterpart including the  return of boss themes and some dialogue  referencing events on Malay Island one  more round it's like a back of Malay  Island the punchline double breaker has  an added function that allows you to  ride it like a skateboard which is  incredibly satisfying to use this isn't  the first time a DMC protagonist has  ridden the brachot though the second  mission cutscene in DMC 3 features Dante  doing the same act of the Cerberus boss  fight  [Music]  the ability to ride the punch line in  this manner is likely a reference to  that over-the-top scene  the devil arm dr. Faust is named after  the Faust the shrouded hat-wearing demon  from DMC for when you acquire the weapon  from Nikko you witness quite a hilarious  fourth wall breaking scene of Dante  dancing like Michael Jackson as strobe  lights flicker and fireworks go off in  the background this scene is likely an  ode to DMC for Dante's ridiculous  shenanigans from his post boss fight  cutscene  Dante has a taunt that pays homage to  the sexual innuendo laced monologue he  delivers after defeating burial in DMC  poor it generally triggers when you  achieve an s-rank you'll know when  you've done it when he throws a rose and  says and that wraps up all the Easter  eggs and references we got but were  there any that you noticed that we  didn't mention here let us know in the  comments anyway go play more Devil May  Cry 5 thanks for watching  [Music]
 

